course: dictionary
lesson: 6862
title: A coat worn over your coat
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Look at the parts of a word. Over means on top, and coat is the thing you wear on your body, so an overcoat is a coat you wear over your other clothes. Check it in the story: the Rat is «restless, overcoat on and pistols in his belt», so he is dressed to go out.
explain: Clues around the word also help. Toad comes down the steps in «an enormous overcoat», with goggles, cap and gauntlets. Goggles and gauntlets are for cold, windy travel, so the overcoat must be a big, warm coat for cold weather.
explain: Overcoat is an old-fashioned word. People today more often say coat or winter coat, but they mean the same thing.
fact: An overcoat is a long, warm coat worn over other clothes in cold weather.
fact: «Overcoat» is a noun. Its plural is overcoats.
fact: In old books and pictures, gentlemen often wear heavy overcoats in winter.
fact: An ulster is a long overcoat, as in «your acquaintance in the large-pattern leather ulster».
fact: Today people usually say coat or winter coat, because overcoat sounds old-fashioned.
exercise: «Back in the kitchen the Rat is restless, overcoat on and pistols in his belt.» What is an overcoat? | A kind of small boat | *A long, warm coat worn over other clothes | A tiny hat worn in summer | A pair of boots for walking in the rain
exercise: Toad comes out in «an enormous overcoat». What is the overcoat for? | *Keeping warm over other clothes in cold weather, not for swimming | Cooling down in the summer sun | Keeping warm over other clothes in cold weather | Carrying food to the river
exercise: Lily says overcoat is an old-fashioned word. What do people often say instead? | Gauntlets | Gloves | *Winter coat | Goggles
test: Toad wears goggles, a cap, gaiters, gauntlets and an overcoat. Which item is worn over the other clothes in cold weather? | Goggles | *Overcoat | Gauntlets | Cap
test: The Rat is «restless, overcoat on» in the kitchen. What does this tell you? | The Rat is asleep in bed | *The Rat is dressed to go out into the cold | The Rat is sad and tired | The Rat has just had a bath
exam: Using the clues around it, what does «overcoat» mean in the story? | *A long, warm coat worn over other clothes | A tool for the garden | A tiny hat worn in summer | A pair of boots
